    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263-a1">

                <pb facs="0317" n="1051" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1051"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 411.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Señor Larrabrue to Mr. Neill.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office of Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1892</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have again forwarded to
                    the marine and treasury offices the contents of your esteemed note of the 27th
                    ultimo, to which I have the honor to reply, and I have strongly asked for a
                    reply regarding the matter you mention of the Hydrographic Commission of the
                    Amazon claim, to which end I have repeated the contents of the official notes
                    directed by this office to the said departments on the 20th of August and the 2d
                    of October, 1891, and the 5th of April of the present year.</p>
                <p>I hope soon to receive the information repeatedly asked for, in order to enable
                    me to give you an answer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Larrabrue y Unanne.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
